  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kungahara Wagura Amasoko (KWA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Rwanda):  ..The Feed the Future (FtF) Kungahara Wagura Amasako (&apos;Prosper While Expanding Markets&apos;) aims to attract investment in export-oriented agricultural value chains and reduce policy and non-tariff barriers that impede the growth of export-oriented agribusinesses. Specifically, the activity will: 1) provide technical assistance to the private sector and Government of Rwanda (GOR) institutions to conduct evidence-based analysis and apply it to policy decisions; 2) provide capacity building to the private sector to advocate for better business policies and regulations; and, 3) develop GOR&apos;s staff technical skills and strengthen their institutional capacity to develop innovative, blended financing instruments to promote increased investments for exports of high-value agriculture and processed foods. . .$1.2 million of funding within this activity contributes to meeting the required &quot;Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSME)&quot; earmark of $9.6 million. The activity is allocating $300,000 to promote gender equality and women empowerment initiatives, through the Gender Equity and Equality Action (GEEA) Fund. The activity closely aligns to GEEA Priority 4: Promote Entrepreneurship, and Financial and Digital Inclusion, including through Trade and Investment..Kungahara Wagura Amasako contributes to USAID&apos;s Country Development Cooperation Strategy Objective 3, &quot;Increase Inclusive and Sustainable Private Sector Driven Growth&quot; and to USAID&apos;s Global Food Security Strategy. ...... .</narrative>
  </description>
